<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Chandawar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1194">1194</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Chandawar was fought in 1194 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a>, in the area of modern Firozabad in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, between the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> and the Gahadavala king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayachandra">Jayachandra</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>. Jayachandra was killed, reportedly struck by an arrow, and his forces broke. The victory opened the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Varanasi</a>, to Ghurid conquest and later to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p></div>
